        "heading": "Tackling Sri Lanka's textile waste mountains",
        "text": "<p>At the heart of our mission is the belief that social and environmental responsibility are inseparable. We create innovative, sustainable design solutions that prioritize the well-being of people, the planet, and our ecosystems. Guided by the principles of reclaiming, reusing and repurposing we craft beautiful, functional products that make a positive impact.</p><p>Sri Lanka’s textile industry produces over 30,000 tonnes of waste annually with over 300 factories operating in the garment industry. AMESH secondary textiles are sourced as pre-consumer textiles and waste materials collected locally. Every piece we create is made from upcycled, deadstock, and end-roll materials, along with trims salvaged from Sri Lanka’s textile markets—materials once discarded as waste and destined for landfills. Through thoughtful reconditioning, reprinting, and embellishment techniques, we breathe new life into these resources, transforming them into unique, one-of-a-kind products.</p>"
