        "heading": "Responsible production",
        "text": "<p>AMESH is on a continuous journey of exploring innovative approaches to sourcing, making, and crafting. With “resourcefulness” at its core, the brand reimagines traditional artisan techniques through refined detailing, vibrant colour, and a celebration of homemaking. Studio leftovers are re-woven into new textures and patterns, turning waste into beauty.</p><p>In partnership with local SMEs, AMESH ensures fair compensation above industry standards, fostering financial stability for its makers. A flexible, work-from-home model supports craftswomen—particularly mothers—enabling them to balance work and family life.</p><p>The brand rejects mass production in favour of limited-edition capsule collections, offering trans-seasonal pieces designed for a shared wardrobe concept. AMESH exists to educate, empower, and inspire a new Sri Lankan identity.</p>"
